  clock: 4  # dcdb
  nonce: dcdb  # dcdb
  message: "Merged in PR #1417 (dev c5249c1aa1).\n\nFixed on branch jgstern-agent/fix/audit0021-rows, commit 7fa77400a5. The six rows are deleted: python logging.basicConfig/StreamHandler, go log/slog.NewTextHandler/NewJSONHandler, elixir Logger.metadata/configure. Each configures or constructs a facility and writes nothing at the call (ADR-0050 axiom). The later emitter is rowed, so the crossing stays represented (ADR-0049 ruling 3; erlang io_lib precedent).\n\nBehavioral evidence: `io-boundaries` on a one-file program per language. Before: logging = {logging.StreamHandler, logging.basicConfig, logging.info} and {Logger.configure, Logger.info, Logger.metadata}. After: logging = {logging.info} and {Logger.info}, with the controls still reported. The go/elixir calls are now reported as external_potential; python's are examined negatives under the `logging` completeness grant, whose note now says so (test_audit0021_adjacent_rows.py::TestWiRagazConfiguringAFacilityWritesNothing).\n\nCorpus A/B: full-stack-fastapi-template logging.basicConfig 4→0. Logger.configure/metadata moved from logging to external_potential on phoenix-framework, plausible-analytics, livebook and emqx. One host_secret→logging flow was lost on phoenix-framework (Application.get_env → Logger.configure in with_logger_app); it was read and is a config restore, not a log write. No verdict moved toward confirmed.\n\nNOT asserted: any corpus effect of the go rows (0 reach in the cohort). Residuals filed as WI-nikir: basicConfig(filename=...) file creation (13/477 corpus calls), and values carried through facility state."  # dcdb
